      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory RTO Paperwork, Transit Marine Insurance &amp; Delivery Handover for Transportation 8409531615</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;">
	<p>When it comes to transporting your car safely and securely, it is crucial to have the right documentation in place.</p>

	<p>The car's Registration Certificate (RC) plays a vital role in car transportation. A self-attested photocopy of the RC is essential to prove the ownership of the vehicle. In Rau, it is crucial to have this document ready beforehand.</p>

	<p>To ensure that your car is in compliance with the pollution control norms, it is necessary to have a valid Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate. A current PUC certificate will be required during car transportation in Rau.</p>

	<p>A valid insurance certificate is essential for car transportation. It provides financial protection in case of any accident or damage during the transportation process. Ensure that you have an up-to-date and valid insurance certificate before the car is transported in Rau.</p>

	<p>To ensure a hassle-free car transportation experience, it is advisable to use an IBA (Indian Bureau of Agreement) approved consignment bill of lading. This document serves as a contract between you and the car transportation company, outlining the details of the car and transportation terms.</p>
	<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px;">
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #f59e0b22; color: #f59e0b; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">01</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Vehicle Details:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The bill of lading should include information such as the car's make, model, color, and any additional specifications.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Transportation Details:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The bill of lading should mention the transportation mode (road, rail, or both), pick-up and delivery locations, dates, and any special requirements.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Insurance Details:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The bill of lading should clearly state the insurance coverage provided, including the amount of protection offered and the insurance company's details.</p>
  </div>
</div>

	<p>To ensure maximum protection for your car during transportation, it is essential to avail a 100% declared value marine transit insurance. This insurance policy covers any damage or loss during the transportation process.</p>
	<p>The 100% declared value ensures that you receive compensation based on the full value of your car in case of any unfortunate event during transportation. Always ensure that the insurance company is well-known and reliable.</p>

	<p>Before the car is picked up for transportation, it is advisable to get a Vehicle Inspection Report (VIR) done. This report provides a detailed assessment of the car's condition and highlights any existing damages or issues.</p>
	<p>The VIR serves as a record of the car's condition before transportation, ensuring that any new damages or issues can be identified and claimed for during the transportation process.</p>

	<p>Upon delivery of the car, it is crucial to get a Car Condition Report (CCR) done.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



